# Filament conventions

## Resources

- One `Resource` per model under `app/Filament/Resources/`
- Pages in `{Resource}/Pages/` (List, Create, Edit, View as needed)
- Relation managers in `{Resource}/RelationManagers/`
- Delegate business logic to `App\Services\api\v1\*` — resources wire UI only

## Table actions → dedicated classes

Do **not** inline complex `Action::make()` logic in resources. Use classes under `app/Filament/Actions/`:

| Kind | Path examples |
|------|----------------|
| Table status actions | `Actions/Status/ApproveAction`, `RejectAction`, `ResetAction` |
| Question-specific | `Actions/Question/ApproveQuestionAction`, `RejectQuestionAction` |
| Form/modal actions | `Actions/Forms/Status/...` |
| Bulk delete | `Actions/Delete/DeleteBulkAction`, `ForceDeleteBulkAction` |

Table actions extend `Filament\Tables\Actions\Action`, call services in `->action()`, check policies with `auth()->user()->can()`.

## Reusable columns & filters

Extract repeated table UI into shared classes:

- **Status column**: `App\Filament\Columns\Status\StatusColumn::make()` — badge + `Status::colorByValue()`
- **Status filter**: `App\Filament\Filters\Status\StatusFilter::make()` — options from `Status::options()`
- **Soft deletes**: `App\Filament\Filters\Trash\TrashedFilter::make()`
- **Forms**: `App\Filament\Forms/Status/StatusSelect`, notification helpers in `Forms/Notification/`

Register in resource `table()`:

```php
->columns([StatusColumn::make(), /* … */])
->filters([StatusFilter::make(), TrashedFilter::make()])
```

## Status workflow

Models implementing `App\Interfaces\v1\Status\StatusInterface` use shared status actions (`ApproveAction`, etc.) and `StatusService` for transitions. Hide actions when `!$record->can('changeStatus')` or terminal state (e.g. `isApproved()`).

## Widgets & infolists

- Widgets: `app/Filament/Resources/Widgets/` or `Resources/{Resource}/Widgets/`
- Custom pages: `app/Filament/Pages/` (e.g. settings, mass notifications)

## Traits

Shared form/table behavior: `app/Traits/Filament/` (e.g. `WithRelatedSelects`).
